AC"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nMax Weber famously wrote that politics is \"a strong and slow boring of hard boards.\" In [Why it took 4 years to get a lock files specification](https://snarky.ca/why-it-took-4-years-to-get-a-lock-files-specification/), Brett Cannon demonstrates how the same principle applies to technical coordination in open source.\n\nPython recently adopted [PEP 751](https://peps.python.org/pep-0751/) for lockfile specification. Doing so","key":"GMQXEcgCzd"}],"key":"F0NAyOnOWT"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"eHmeh5Fywb"}],"key":"Eyb7UWxtHz"},{"type":"text","value":"October 21, 2025 | ","key":"jM1WrR3PZm"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"Bp1ke0p9JU"}],"key":"VdQNw4ZNnR"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"DypYRPUfOt"}],"key":"oUOajAY0MA"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/lock-files","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.lock-files.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"GWspAfBswt"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"My system for beating jet lag","key":"VEJhUIhkoX"}],"key":"juPOv3G5Yt"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nI travel internationally a lot, which means I deal with a lot of jet lag. This post is a quick summary of a system I've found helpful, based on [this paper](https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fphys.2019.00927/full).\n\n\nThe basic idea is to shift your body's internal clock by timing your exposure to light, exercise, and melatonin around","key":"fUXI5KQdOy"}],"key":"zU8SWj2doZ"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"JaE1PFul7t"}],"key":"OmbxPsxyIO"},{"type":"text","value":"October 18, 2025 | ","key":"Y4QV38FlLA"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"IpBIAov4QQ"}],"key":"yzI5JsjH3P"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"O3EAM54K7k"}],"key":"C05ujb9Xga"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.jet-lag.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"OSoDK4NgUA"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why open source foundations try to fund systems, not development","key":"V7nz22bAIw"}],"key":"MUp0ANTkUY"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\nThis is a brief reflection on something that I've been hearing consistently from the Linux Foundation and its member projects as part of serving on the [Board of the Jupyter Foundation](https://jupyterfoundation.org). Here's a point that originally surprised me when I heard it:\n\n> Most foundations within the Linux Foundation network recommend","key":"ovTlFVMDAb"}],"key":"D9Mx0KLnrc"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"toWiT8cvgp"}],"key":"FviVTuJzsG"},{"type":"text","value":"May 31, 2025 | ","key":"J0mTKoqyHL"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"moNzIcd9Q1"}],"key":"EbUvXt9kde"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"ViNU1VAGQe"}],"key":"V6sv8Bz1OC"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.fund-systems-not-developmend.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"UKN8Ef1LbR"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Jupyter can align the needs of its community and its foundation by enabling contribution","key":"egnj9Jk1SZ"}],"key":"hAKQIeahZU"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThis week was my first time attending the [Linux Foundation Member Summit](https://events.linuxfoundation.org/lf-member-summit/). This is an annual meeting for all of the Linux Foundation member organizations and projects. I joined because of my new role [on the Jupyter Executive Council](./jec.md), and so I tried to go into this meeting with the","key":"Ldo8aCHKaZ"}],"key":"T4rNKSj2rH"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"O7OWOclteG"}],"key":"GE2bZJ3yzs"},{"type":"text","value":"March 22, 2025 | ","key":"YKtNj5TAOk"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"QB8CJIPyPJ"}],"key":"M2uLTQMXPH"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"TVGqwfE0qs"}],"key":"Kxlcr91FLa"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.more-contributors.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"L6jHKW6Q41"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The relationship between the Jupyter Executive Council, Software Steering Council, and Foundation","key":"HQm2gYHy50"}],"key":"M2Byjv60Ry"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis is a question that I've been asked many times now that I'm serving on the ","key":"JMVsn8Sdaf"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"Jupyter Executive Council","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JEC","key":"ESO6PeFAvy"}],"key":"b7ZvToILFT"},{"type":"text","value":" and the ","key":"L1HWKDowb8"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"The Jupyter Foundation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JF","key":"VpKZI1STpq"}],"key":"d4gGVCpTHF"},{"type":"text","value":". I'm writing up a quick response so that I have something to refer back to and align my own thinking on.\n\n**How most Linux Foundation projects seem to be structured**. Linux","key":"QyECT5dZKk"}],"key":"oiwZT13DC7"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"pLUZqZ4Cim"}],"key":"b0MYH5EcFe"},{"type":"text","value":"March 02, 2025 | ","key":"n1LVaECUFX"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"GZWmWz8C3W"}],"key":"csrqP3dZ5M"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"GxP53Qo49o"}],"key":"ph3oDxj66d"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.jupyter-org-structure.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"tkBiEC3Luk"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/os-support","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ways the Jupyter Foundation could support open source projects","key":"ArRfbzn1kI"}],"key":"GLHF427uDp"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThe Jupyter Foundation has a pot of money and it aims to use that funding quickly to support the Jupyter Project. But what should it use the funding _for_? There are many things to do, and not enough time or money to try everything. This is a brief brainstorm and","key":"Z3m8ycVnRv"}],"key":"CS8rBOrpuH"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"UFMtAKdI7r"}],"key":"rE3vP0W3Jw"},{"type":"text","value":"February 26, 2025 | ","key":"qfj0yrUn0H"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"BI05lU3R9Y"}],"key":"t2MbIxSXPN"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"h28rpmXeQC"}],"key":"o5ttOzT9QT"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/os-support","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.os-support.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"sBIRIkDLC8"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jec","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why I'm running for the Jupyter Executive Council","key":"lzO39af4Rk"}],"key":"BgfgDhAhx2"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis year, I decided to nominate myself for the [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html). This is a brief post explaining my rationale for doing so, the kind of service I'd hope to provide the project, and where I imagine the project moving.\n\n\nThe [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html) is the highest governing body within the","key":"HLH7qu0gc1"}],"key":"dJZedH0BQ3"},{"type":"f